.TH "SSOOSSH" "1" "Aug 2026" "ssoossh" ""

.SH NAME
ssoossh-ssh-proxycommand - Ensure a valid certificate, then relay stdio to the target host over TCP.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh ssh proxycommand [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
For use as ssh_config's ProxyCommand. Arguments after ProxyCommand should mirror exactly as if you weren't calling ssoossh.

.PP
from ssh_config man page
Before: ProxyCommand /usr/bin/nc -X connect -x 192.0.2.0:8080 %h %p
After : ProxyCommand gendocs ssh ProxyCommand /usr/bin/nc -X connect -x 192.0.2.0:8080 %h %p

.PP
NOTICE: Use of ssh key files will not work here as ssh only reads them once at start and will not see our changes to them.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for proxycommand


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


